From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoCo starter <coco-starter@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:54:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] null: write every rendered frame to a stream

When the COCO_FRAMES environment variable names a path, append every
frame that the null UI's software renderer completes to it as a binary
PPM, the same format as the single COCO_VIDEO frame. The path can be a
named pipe to an encoder that reads a stream of PPM images, so a long
recording needs no disk space for raw frames.

Logs COCO_FRAMES_START,<tick>,<ticks per second>,<width>,<height>
before the first frame and COCO_FRAME,<tick> after each frame, so that
the frame rate and the offset from the audio recording come from the
emulator's own clock. If the viewport size changes during a recording,
XRoar logs COCO_FRAMES_SIZE,<width>,<height> and exits.

Without COCO_FRAMES nothing is written.

This is test equipment for the CoCo starter's scripts/coco.py.
